[[ ## document ## ]]
{
  "title": "FY2026 Audit Calendar — Harbor Light Engagement",
  "path": "Audit/FY2026/Harbor_Light/Audit_Calendar_FY2026.docx",
  "document": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "text": "FY2026 Audit Calendar — Harbor Light Engagement"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Prepared by: Imogen Carraway, Audit Manager | Date: Post-season planning | Status: Draft for partner review"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "1. Engagement Overview"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "This calendar integrates the Harbor Light FY2026 audit (year-end 31 December 2026) with the firm's policy frameworks: engagement letter, PBC request, time & billing, tax return workflow, and the current rate sheet. Dates assume standard staffing levels and no scope changes from FY2025."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "2. Key Dates and Milestones"
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Milestone", "Date", "Owner", "Reference Policy"],
        "rows": [
          ["Engagement letter issued to client", "15 Jan 2026", "Partner (R. Okafor)", "Engagement letter policy — §2.1"],
          ["Engagement letter signed and returned", "12 Feb 2026", "Client", "Engagement letter policy — §2.3"],
          ["PBC request sent to client", "16 Feb 2026", "Imogen Carraway", "PBC request policy — §3.1"],
          ["PBC due date (client to submit)", "31 Mar 2026", "Client", "PBC request policy — §3.4"],
          ["Interim fieldwork (planning, risk assessment)", "20–24 Apr 2026", "Imogen + Staff 1", "Firm audit methodology"],
          ["Time & billing setup / budget load", "30 Apr 2026", "Billing coordinator", "Time & billing policy — §4.2"],
          ["Tax return data request to client (FY2026 estimate)", "15 May 2026", "Tax manager (S. Patel)", "Tax return workflow — §5.1"],
          ["Final fieldwork (year-end testing)", "11–22 Jan 2027", "Imogen + Staff 2", "Firm audit methodology"],
          ["Tax return draft to client for review", "29 Jan 2027", "S. Patel", "Tax return workflow — §5.4"],
          ["Review notes cleared", "5 Feb 2027", "Imogen", "Quality review policy"],
          ["Draft financial statements to client", "12 Feb 2027", "Imogen", "Reporting policy — §6.2"],
          ["Client approval of financial statements", "19 Feb 2027", "Client", "Reporting policy — §6.3"],
          ["Tax return filed (extension not expected)", "28 Feb 2027", "S. Patel", "Tax return workflow — §5.6"],
          ["Audit report signed and issued", "28 Feb 2027", "Partner", "Reporting policy — §6.5"],
          ["Time & billing close-out (all time posted, billed)", "15 Mar 2027", "Billing coordinator", "Time & billing policy — §4.7"],
          ["Post-season wrap-up / next-year planning", "30 Mar 2027", "Imogen", "Firm planning cycle"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "3. PBC Request Details (issued 16 Feb 2026)"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The PBC request will be sent via the client portal, with the following categories (mirroring FY2025 structure):"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "Trial balance as of 31 Dec 2026 (with prior-year comparatives)",
          "General ledger detail for all accounts with activity > $10,000",
          "Bank statements and confirmations (all accounts)",
          "Accounts receivable aging as of year-end",
          "Accounts payable detail and open invoices",
          "Fixed asset rollforward and depreciation schedule",
          "Debt schedules and loan agreements",
          "Revenue contracts and deferred revenue analysis",
          "Payroll reports (including 941s and state filings)",
          "Board minutes and related-party disclosures"
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "4. Budget and Rate Assumptions"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Based on the current rate sheet (effective 1 Jan 2026) and FY2025 actual hours, the preliminary budget is as follows. Rates are standard and have been held flat from FY2025."
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Staff Level", "Rate/hr (USD)", "Budgeted Hours", "Budgeted Fee"],
        "rows": [
          ["Partner", "350", "40", "14,000"],
          ["Audit Manager (Imogen)", "275", "120", "33,000"],
          ["Senior Associate", "190", "160", "30,400"],
          ["Staff Associate", "135", "200", "27,000"],
          ["TOTAL", "—", "520", "104,400"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Hourly budgets are preliminary and will be loaded into the time & billing system by 30 Apr 2026. Any scope change requiring more than a 10% overrun must be approved by the engagement partner and communicated to the client in writing."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "5. Tax Return Workflow Integration"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The tax return (Form 1120 — Harbor Light is a C-corporation) runs in parallel with the audit. The tax manager will receive a copy of the PBC request to avoid duplicate information requests. Key dependencies:"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          "Tax data request issued 15 May 2026 (estimate-based) so the client can assemble book-tax differences during the year.",
          "Final tax figures will use the audited financial statements (draft available 12 Feb 2027).",
          "The tax return is due 28 Feb 2027; no extension is planned. If the client delays the PBC submission beyond 31 Mar 2026, the tax filing date will be re-assessed.",
          "Any federal or state filing deadline changes will be tracked in the firm's compliance calendar."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "6. Assumptions and Risks"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "Client submits all PBC items by 31 Mar 2026. A late submission compresses interim fieldwork and may require an extension of the final audit window.",
          "Staffing is assumed at 2 staff members (one senior, one associate) plus the manager and partner. If a staff member is reassigned, the calendar shifts by up to 1 week.",
          "The rate sheet is assumed to remain unchanged through Feb 2027. If rates change, the budget will be updated at interim.",
          "No significant scope changes (e.g., new debt covenants, related-party transactions) are anticipated. Any such changes will trigger a revised engagement letter.",
          "The client's fiscal year-end remains 31 December. Any change would invalidate this calendar."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "7. Approvals"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "This draft calendar is for partner review. Upon approval, it will be shared with the client as an informational timeline and with the audit team as the working schedule."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Imogen Carraway\nAudit Manager, Senior"
      }
    ]
  }
}
